sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In a Markov-chain model of transitions between movement types, circular motion is the most persistent Anthrobot behaviour, followed by linear and curvilinear motion, while eclectic motion acts as a transient intermediate that probabilistically resolves into one of the other three types.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Circular motion is the most stable Anthrobot behaviour; eclectic motion is transient";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Gumuskaya G, Srivastava P, Cooper BG, Lesser H, Semegran B, Garnier S, Levin M, “Motile Living Biobots Self-Construct from Adult Human Somatic Progenitor Seed Cells”, Advanced science (Weinheim, Baden-Wurttemberg, Germany) (2024), doi:10.1002/advs.202303575; section “Results › Anthrobots Self‐Organize into Discrete Movement Types”. Scope: NHBE-derived Anthrobots, 30 s trajectory segments over 5 h"
}
